Error [jet.UseAfterMove]: `evens` was consumed by the assignment to `kept`, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/assignment_move_use_after_move.jet:8:11
    |
  8 |     print(evens.to_list())
    |           ^^^^^
  --> tests/ui/assignment_move_use_after_move.jet:6:12
    |
  6 |     kept = evens
    |            ^^^^^ `evens` moved to the assignment to `kept` here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `evens` after the move, or give the assignment to `kept` a copy with `evens.copy()` where it moved.
 Note: `evens` is one-pass — materialize it first with `evens.to_list()`, or create a fresh source for the second drive
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
